---
// Career + education. Outcome-first bullets.
---

<section id="experience" class="sec on-ink">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>Career</h2>
    </div>

    <ol class="career">
      <li class="spell">
        <p class="when cap">Jun 2025 – Dec 2025</p>
        <div>
          <h3>Business Systems Analyst Intern</h3>
          <p class="club cap">PCL Construction · Edmonton, AB</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Shipped a <strong>production AI agent</strong> (Microsoft Copilot + LLM prompting)
              that automates retrieval of institutional knowledge across business units,
              wiring SharePoint and Azure Blob Storage into a <strong>RAG</strong> pipeline.
            </li>
            <li>
              Owned it end-to-end — requirements, user testing, deployment — and built
              <strong>Python APIs</strong> feeding live operational data into daily reports.
            </li>
            <li>
              Placed <strong>3rd company-wide</strong> in PCL's BT AI Challenge,
              competing against full-time professionals.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="spell">
        <p class="when cap">Jul 2023 – Dec 2023</p>
        <div>
          <h3>Data &amp; Operations Analyst Intern</h3>
          <p class="club cap">Safety First Industrial Inc. · Sherwood Park, AB</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Designed an end-to-end <strong>ETL pipeline</strong> in Python consolidating
              multiple source systems into a central SQL database —
              <strong>eliminating ~6 hours of manual work every week</strong>.
            </li>
            <li>
              Built a validation utility catching cross-system inconsistencies,
              improving data integrity <strong>~30%</strong> upstream of every report.
            </li>
            <li>
              Served as the site's <strong>sole technical resource</strong>, automating
              workflows across SharePoint, Sage 50, and Shopify with Python and PowerShell.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="spell">
        <p class="when cap">2021 – Present</p>
        <div>
          <h3>BSc Computing Science, Business Minor</h3>
          <p class="club cap">University of Alberta · Edmonton, AB</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Gold Standard in Science</strong> (2021) ·
              <strong>Undergraduate Leadership Award</strong> (2022)
            </li>
            <li>
              Machine Learning, Applied Statistics, Database Management,
              Software Engineering, Data Structures &amp; Algorithms.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .career { list-style: none; border-top: 2px solid var(--n1); }
  .spell {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 220px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 12px clamp(20px, 4vw, 56px);
    padding: 36px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--n8);
  }
  .when {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--n3);
    padding-top: 6px;
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.4vw, 1.95rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-stretch: 88%;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--n0);
  }
  .club { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--n4); }
  ul { list-style: none; margin-top: 20px; display: grid; gap: 12px; max-width: 72ch; }
  li li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 26px;
    color: var(--n4);
  }
  li li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.62em;
    width: 12px;
    height: 4px;
    background: var(--cobalt);
    clip-path: polygon(3px 0, 100% 0, calc(100% - 3px) 100%, 0 100%);
  }
  strong { color: var(--n0); font-weight: 700; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .spell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: 28px 0; }
    .when { padding-top: 0; }
  }
</style>
